  <metadata>
    <name>Rothay Riverside Loop</name>
    <desc>6.8 km with 95 m of climb. From the Bracken Fell Harriers route book.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <trk>
    <name>Rothay Riverside Loop</name>
    <desc>The club's default easy evening: out along the River Rothay, around the Under Loughrigg lane and back over the stone footbridge. Barely a climb worth naming, though the two short rises past Fox How will still say hello. Runnable end to end in road shoes unless the river has been up.</desc>
